generated_hash =

// @vibe/compiler/core — ADR-0070 / #897 compiler-internal contract. This is
// the LAST plain directory under lib/@vibe/compiler/ and the highest-risk
// one: it owns the central type-system enums (`Type`/`TypeDef`/`TypeEnv`/
// `Subst`, types.vibe) and re-exports the surface-syntax AST enums
// (`Expr`/`Pat`/`Stmt`/`TypeExpr`) from the external @vibe/ast contract
// package. All eight enums are pattern-matched and constructed EVERYWHERE
// across the compiler (checker, codegen, normalize, perceus, every other
// already-migrated package), so this header documents the type-declaration
// reasoning in more depth than usual.
//
// Directory-shared-scope package (7 impl files + the facade): ast.vibe
// (cross-package re-export shim, see below), bytebuf.vibe (wasm
// bytecode-buffer / leb128 helpers), dce.vibe (dead-code elimination over
// Stmt), polyfill.vibe (__to_string), sorted_index.vibe (sorted-name-table
// binary search helpers), import_alias_rewrite.vibe (import-alias rewriting
// + the whole-program export-rename plan), types.vibe (the type-system
// core: unification, generalization, trait resolution, ...).
//
// -- Two-tier type-declaration strategy --
//
// (1) Expr/Pat/Stmt/TypeExpr: ast.vibe re-exports these from the EXTERNAL
// @vibe/ast package (`export ../../../../lib/@vibe/ast { Expr, Pat, Stmt,
// TypeExpr }`, rewritten from a bare `import {...}` + `export {...}`
// two-step that does NOT satisfy check_contract as an implementation --
// only a real local `export fn`/`export type` body or an SReExport counts).
// They are declared BODYLESS here (`type Expr`, not a transparent copy of
// @vibe/ast/index.vpkg's full enum bodies), mirroring syntax/index.vpkg's
// identical `type Token` declaration for its own cross-package re-export of
// @vibe/parser's Token. check_contract trusts a re-exported name at face
// value (no body/arity comparison at all, see check_contract's `reexported`
// handling in contract/contract.vibe) -- @vibe/ast/index.vpkg is what
// actually pins Expr/Pat/Stmt/TypeExpr's shape, this contract only needs to
// vouch that core/ makes the name available.
//
// (2) Type/TypeDef/TypeEnv/Subst: these are core/'s OWN definitions (real
// `export enum` bodies in types.vibe, not a re-export), yet they are ALSO
// declared BODYLESS here (`type Type`, not transparent), NOT full enum
// bodies. This looks counterintuitive for a type this heavily pattern
// -matched, but it is the established, triple-precedented pattern for
// exactly this shape ("transparent enum with a REAL body already living in
// a sibling impl file"):
//   - @vibe/parser/index.vpkg's `type Token`: "a transparent contract
//     definition would hit the impl-before-facade check order, #752 rule"
//   - checker/index.vpkg's `type EffectError`: bodyless despite
//     checker_effects.vibe constructing/matching it constantly
//   - perceus/index.vpkg's `opaque type PerceusActionKind`: "enum VARIANTS
//     do not resolve across units from a facade-only definition (@vibe/json
//     precedent -- 'unknown name: JNull')... consumers keep full variant
//     visibility through the same #716 re-export machinery as before"
// A FULL transparent body is only correct when the contract IS the sole
// source of the definition (@vibe/ast/index.vpkg's own Pat/Expr/Stmt/
// TypeExpr: their impl file, ast.vibe, is an empty stub). Since types.vibe
// independently carries the real `export enum Type { ... }` etc. bodies,
// putting the same bodies here too would duplicate the definition through
// the generated facade (the impl-before-facade hazard above) rather than
// widen or change the surface. Bodyless declarations here do not narrow
// what downstream consumers can do: check_contract/collect_impl_type_defs
// still validates arity (0 for all four) against types.vibe's real defs,
// and actual pattern-matching/construction resolves through the ordinary
// dependency closure to types.vibe's real bodies -- proven by contract.vibe
// itself already pattern-matching @vibe/parser's Token (also bodyless in
// its origin contract) today.
//
// ExportRenamePlan (import_alias_rewrite.vibe) is declared fully `opaque`
// (not even bodyless-transparent): no external caller accesses its fields
// via dot-notation, every consumer goes through the accessor fns
// (export_plan_renames_for, export_plan_rename_count,
// export_plan_fingerprint_text, collect_import_value_renames), so the
// struct's field layout is not part of the public surface (@vibe/compiler/
// perceus's `PCtx`-not-declared caution: do not widen the surface beyond
// what was already reachable through the old plain index.vibe facade).
//
// Naming: no collision on the established `git mv index.vibe <dirname>.vibe`
// convention -- core/core.vibe did not exist, so the old facade moved
// verbatim to core.vibe (its own re-export blocks, including the pre-#897
// `export ./ast.vibe { Expr, Pat, Stmt, TypeExpr }` line, are left
// untouched and are no longer load-bearing for outside importers now that
// this contract's generated facade is the source of truth -- same
// non-load-bearing-old-facade shape as checker_facade.vibe). ast.vibe is
// listed BEFORE core.vibe below so ast.vibe's own re-export claims
// Expr/Pat/Stmt/TypeExpr first in facade generation; core.vibe's
// already-redundant re-export of the same names is simply skipped (already
// allocated), exactly like checker_facade.vibe's redundant re-export block.
//
// No import cycle: core/'s only compiler-internal dependency (beyond its
// own siblings) is ../module_graph_path.vibe (a top-level compiler file,
// imported by import_alias_rewrite.vibe), which itself only imports the
// external @vibe/core package -- it does not import core/ back.

